    {
      "kind": "BRUTE_FORCE",
      "language": "JAVASCRIPT",
      "title": "Every pair of endpoints",
      "intuition": "Each trail is the unique path between two nodes, so measure the path sum from every node to every other node.",
      "approach": "Build an undirected adjacency list. From each node, run a DFS accumulating sums along the way and track the maximum.",
      "pseudocode": "for start: dfs over the tree without revisiting, sum along the path; best = max(best, sum)",
      "code": "function canopyGain(tree) {\n  const nodes = [];\n  const root = { value: tree[0], left: null, right: null };\n  nodes.push(root);\n  for (let i = 1, head = 0; i < tree.length; head++) {\n    const node = nodes[head];\n    if (tree[i] !== null) nodes.push(node.left = { value: tree[i], left: null, right: null });\n    i++;\n    if (i < tree.length && tree[i] !== null) nodes.push(node.right = { value: tree[i], left: null, right: null });\n    i++;\n  }\n  const adj = new Map(nodes.map((n) => [n, []]));\n  for (const n of nodes) for (const child of [n.left, n.right]) if (child) { adj.get(n).push(child); adj.get(child).push(n); }\n  let best = -Infinity;\n  for (const start of nodes) {\n    const stack = [[start, null, start.value]];\n    while (stack.length) {\n      const [n, from, sum] = stack.pop();\n      best = Math.max(best, sum);\n      for (const m of adj.get(n)) if (m !== from) stack.push([m, n, sum + m.value]);\n    }\n  }\n  return best;\n}",
      "timeComplexity": "O(n²)",
      "spaceComplexity": "O(n)",
      "commonMistakes": [
        "Only considering paths that start at the root."
      ],
      "interviewExplanation": "Every trail is the path between two nodes, so a search from each node covers them all. That's quadratic.",
      "steps": [
